Here is yet another list for fixes for Tim Stoehr's rogue clone.I was not able to contact Tim at his Tektronix email address, soI added these myself.  This introduces a diversion from the rogueclone distributed by Berkeley but I don't really see them as beinginterested in VMS compatability.			Mike Zraly			mzraly@ldbvax.dnet.lotus.com			or c/o seaotter@athena.mit.edu	---------------------------------------------------- 1.)	Add VMS compatability through changes to machdep.c (add	appropriate code), the introduction of one small #define	to rogue.h, and a package of VMS keyboard i/o functions	I developed (vmsterm.c and vmsterm.h).  I also added a	Makefile for VMS suitable for use with the VMS Make program	(available via anonymous FTP from vmsd.oac.uci.edu or	pomona.claremont.edu) 2.)	Replace comment within comment in machdep.c (circa line 41)	with [* ... *] instead of /* ... */ 3.)	Change patchlevel.h 4.)	Change version message in play.c